GIMP Palette
Name: AutoBattler — Tabletop Skirmish
Columns: 4
#
# Direction: a wargame on a felt-topped table, lit from above. The conceit is
# that none of this is happening — they are pieces, and the player is a pair of
# hands, which is exactly what an auto-battler asks of them.
#
# So the units are painted like painted miniatures: three steps, chunky, no
# faces. ally-* and foe-* are the same three-step structure in blue and red,
# because two armies of pieces from one set is the whole point, and any detail
# that made one side more characterful would undercut it.
#
# felt-* is the board and wood-* is the shop frame around it. Keeping those two
# materials distinct is what stops the drag-to-place from feeling like it
# happens nowhere — you are moving a piece from the shelf onto the table.
#
 26  26  26	outline
 30  52  42	felt-0-shadow
 46  80  62	felt-1
 68 112  86	felt-2
 98 148 114	felt-3-hilite
 64  42  28	wood-0-shadow
104  70  44	wood-1
148 104  66	wood-2
198 152 104	wood-3-hilite
 58  70  96	ally-0-shadow
 92 116 160	ally-1
136 166 214	ally-2-hilite
104  44  52	foe-0-shadow
158  62  66	foe-1
212 100  92	foe-2-hilite
230 196 108	gold
238 232 220	bone
